content.text:
Found it. This commit (b83ce94c6) is a refactor that replaced `DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine` calls with `ClipPlayer.play`, and while doing so collapsed the `if/else-if` for combat-move vs non-combat-move sounds into a single `if` with an OR condition — but kept only the `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT` sound and dropped the `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT` branch entirely, along with setting `m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove`. This is exactly the bug that the fix commit (9a02e14) addresses by splitting back into two separate `if` blocks (though the fix itself still mistakenly plays `CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT` in both branches — a separate, lesser issue not part of this investigation).

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: b83ce94c63ec1891f5b76837455c8b2a53ad9d9c

## Reasoning
(1) I ran `git log -p` on `src/games/strategy/triplea/TripleAPlayer.java` and grepped for the relevant symbols (`CLIP_PHASE_MOVE`, `m_soundPlayedAlready`) to trace the history of the buggy conditional across commits.

(2) In commit `b83ce94c6` (Sep 18 2015), the original code was:
```java
if (nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove) {
    DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT, id.getName());
    m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove = true;
} else if (!nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove) {
    DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT, id.getName());
    m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true;
}
```
